# Cloudflare Pages routing — Father Kaz Ligeza
#
# IMPORTANT: this file intentionally contains NO catch-all rewrite.
#
# Per Cloudflare's docs, `_redirects` rules are applied BEFORE static assets and
# are "always followed, regardless of whether or not an asset matches the
# incoming request". A catch-all like:
#
#     /*    /index.html   200
#
# would therefore OVERRIDE the per-route prerendered HTML files emitted by
# scripts/postbuild.mjs (about.html, books/<slug>.html, ...), discarding their
# route-specific <title>/meta/canonical and defeating the prerender.
#
# Because the project ships those static .html files and has no top-level
# 404.html, Cloudflare Pages already:
#   1. serves the matching static file for any real route, and
#   2. falls back to the SPA shell (/index.html) for unmatched paths.
#
# So no rewrite is required here. Add only explicit, intentional rules below if
# a future need arises (e.g. www -> apex is handled via a dashboard Redirect
# Rule, not this file).
